ets paid  848 000 pounds and the ceo of iag  the parent company of british airways  gets paid 4.9 million pounds it's about  the fact that british airways paid 1.6  billion pounds in dividends out to  shareholders when it was profitable  prior to the pandemic instead of  reinvesting that money into its staff  and into things like it systems to make  sure that that that the airline is able  to function properly it's about the fact  that working people have seen the  sharpest decline in their living  standards in two decades and it's about  the fact that working people have had  enough and actually that they see that  there is some hope in standing together  collectively and organizing and if this  is the spark that lights the flame that  leads to worse you there do forgive me  come back and talk to us  next week or whenever you'd like to  thanks very much indeed for joining us  on the program
 

